<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Naveta des Tudons</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Naveta des Tudons is a prehistoric stone tomb near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ciutadella-de-menorca">Ciutadella</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menorca">Menorca</a>, shaped like an upturned boat. Built of large dressed stones without mortar in the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a>, it was a collective burial chamber on two levels, in which the remains of dozens of people were found. It is the best-preserved monument of its kind in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balearic-islands">Balearic Islands</a> and a symbol of Menorca's prehistoric past.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/naveta-des-tudons.jpg" alt="Naveta des Tudons" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tudons01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
